  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 845748,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## Nord and Bert Couldn't Make Head or Tail of It: A Synopsis\n\nStep into the whimsical town of Punster in *Nord and Bert Couldn't Make Head or Tail of It*, a unique text adventure from Infocom where idioms and clichés have sprung to life! This unconventional game, released alongside *Plundered Hearts*, challenges players with a series of eight \"interactive short stories\" centered around wordplay and puns.\n\nThe first seven chapters – \"The Shopping Bizarre,\" \"Playing Jacks,\" \"Buy the Farm,\" \"Eat Your Words,\" \"Act the Part,\" \"Manor of Speaking,\" and \"Shake a Tower\" – can be tackled in any order, each presenting bizarre scenarios demanding clever linguistic solutions. Solve a grocery store riddle by identifying homonyms, literally interpret farm idioms, or navigate a 1950s sitcom with slapstick precision. \n\nGameplay diverges from traditional Infocom adventures; simply typing a location or object name instantly transports you or examines it. The final chapter, \"Meet the Mayor,\" weaves together elements from the previous sections, requiring mastery of puns and a keen understanding of American English. A delightful booklet of wordplay cartoons by Kevin Pope accompanies the game, offering visual clues and adding to the overall charm."
    },
